<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#sesame">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sesame</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sesame is a flowering plant cultivated for its oil-rich seeds, one of the oldest oilseed crops. It was grown widely in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> list sesame among the crops of Mesopotamian agriculture that sustained a dense population and generated taxable surplus.</p></div>
